<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60639" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυκλόθεν</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>from all around</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ὁδὸς περίχει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					7.28
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fract.</u>
				33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				4.6.10
			</span></i> (dub.l.), etc.: c. gen., <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>3 Ki.</u>
				18.32
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Apoc.</u>
				4.3
			</span></i>: c. dat., <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>3 Ki.</u>
				6.5
			</span></i>: spelt <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύκλωθεν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IPE</u>
				12.175
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Olbia</span>), and sts. in codd., but this
			spelling is condemned by <i><span class="en">
				Theognost.
				<u>Can.</u>
				156
			</span></i>, and arose from a supposed connexion with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύκλῳ</span>.</div>
